MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_001: Reading again, eh, Tialla? You meant it when you\nsaid you loved books, then?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_002: Mmhmm...
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_003: You know, I happen to keep one of the largest\nlibraries around. With even a few forbidden reads.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_004: Huh? Really? You have outlawed books in\nyour collection?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_027: You've mentioned that before. Do you really have\noutlawed books in your collection?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_005: Well, of course! Am I not the chief executive of \nVandahl Trading?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_006: I can't believe there are forbidden books outside\nthe temples.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_007: What titles do you have? Oh, just thinking about it\nmakes my heart beat faster. I want to read them all!
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_008: Well, they're pretty valuable finds. But I suppose a\nlight tour couldn't hurt. Would you like to go?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_009: Can we?!
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_010: Alright, why the hell not? I've never met someone\nso excited to read a book.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_011: You're brave not to worry though. Folks who travel\nwith me either love danger, or love...well, me.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_012: Worry? Why should I worry? What are you up to?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_013: Just so you know, my heart belongs to Cai.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_014: HA! Tsk, tsk. A guy like me, losing out to a kid like\nCai... How will I possibly recover?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_015: You know you're too old for me, right?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_016: You know, my heart might have just broken there\nif I didn't absolutely agree with you.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_017: Trust me, when it comes to that kind of thing, \nyou have nothing to worry about.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_018: Well! I'm very glad to hear that, mister.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_019: Clever, upfront... You know, Tialla, you're pretty \nsharp...for a kid.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_020: And you're full of surprises...for an adult.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_021: Why, thanks for noticing! It's curiosity that keeps one\nfrom truly growing old, you see.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_022: Anyway, I meant it when I mentioned danger.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_023: My bookshelves may hold knowledge you're happier\nnot knowing.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_024: But if you're feeling brave, come find me. I'll show\nyou those old tomes, just as promised.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_025: I'm up to the challenge.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_C_026: In fact, nothing can hold me back.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_001: There you go, Ms. Tialla. Behold the treasured\nvolumes of the Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_002: Hey, don't tease me, Tali— Oh, this is amazing.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_003: It is, isn't it? And this, here, is only a small part of\nmy collection!
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_004: I can't believe this entire collection belongs to one\nperson. Oh, I'm definitely starting with this one.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_005: Hm, that one is... Ah, yes, Carving Arcs: Trials and\nTribulations.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_006: People will do anything for power, even if the risks\ninclude losing your body forever.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_007: Oh, there are so many examples of people ruining\ntheir bodies here.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_008: Here, we have a record of Sai customs. Oh! And this\nbook of rituals is said to drive its readers insane!
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_009: There's always this one. A study on livestock\nanatomy. A good read, but with such...vivid images.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_010: The temples prohibit unwarranted dissection of\ncarcasses, don't they?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_011: True. Supposedly, the images were drawn mostly\nfrom imagination, but we might never know for sure.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_012: Recording temple knowledge carries a steep\npunishment.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_013: Perhaps. But who knows how much knowledge is\nhidden out there between forbidden pages.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_014: The world you know is just the shiny surface.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_015: Those books will show you the depths. Not for casual\nreading. Scared yet, Tialla?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_016: A-aah...
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_017: Sorry, perhaps bringing you here was all a bit much.\nI did warn you, though...
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_018: Talimun, where are the other books in this set?\nYou do have them, don't you?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_019: Oh? They're over there, but... Wait—really?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_020: You aren't rattled at all, are you? I'd say there's the\nheart of an adventurer in there.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_021: Did you think I wouldn't be able to handle it?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_022: This is one of the reasons I want to do temple work,\nso I can get my hands on books like the ones here.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_023: Well, you've definitely got guts! I should've given\nyou the sales pitch and hired you on!
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_024: Hmmm...a sales pitch, eh?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_025: I don't suppose I could buy this book? Quietly? So the\ntemple doesn't find out?
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_026: Nice try, kid, but this is my prized collection, not\nsome market bookstand.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_027: If I'm buying, I'll take this one, and that related\nvolume, and... Oh, that one looks verrry interesting.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_028: Now, wait a second! I swear, you remind me of that\nstubborn tactician I used to trade with back in Arago.
MID_SE_Tal_Tia_B_029: Alright, fine. You can pick out a FEW. I guess when\nthey say "book-crazy," this is what they mean...